A local-only, single-leg Delhi Metro planning application that uses manually maintained stations, timetable patterns, and public holidays to calculate deterministic crowding predictions, persist matched prediction snapshots, and show an in-app high-crowding advisory.

Design goals:

Support correcting and persisting local station, timetable-pattern, and public-holiday source records.
Derive day type deterministically and match one inclusive local timetable time range.
Persist only matched predictions as immutable historical snapshots.
Show the leave-earlier advisory only for High crowding and only in-app.
Provide explicit validation, empty states, filtering, and chronological result ordering without authentication or external connectivity.
Business rules:

Station names are trimmed, required, and unique by trimmed value. A station referenced by a timetable pattern cannot be deleted.
Timetable patterns require existing distinct station IDs, valid closed day type and crowding values, 24-hour HH:MM times, and start_time earlier than end_time.
Inclusive timetable time ranges cannot overlap for the same origin, destination, and day type; shared endpoints overlap.
Holidays require a YYYY-MM-DD date, a non-blank trimmed display name, and a unique calendar date.
A holiday date is Holiday; a non-holiday Saturday or Sunday is Weekend; all other non-holiday dates are Weekday.
Journey prediction requires existing distinct station IDs, a YYYY-MM-DD journey date, and HH: MM planned departure time.
A match has identical station pair and derived day type, with start_time less than or equal to planned time and end_time greater than or equal to planned time.
A matched prediction uses the matched pattern baseline crowding and saves a snapshot of station names and derived journey facts. A no-match prediction is not saved.
Only High matched predictions set is_leave_earlier_alert_shown to true. Their alert text is Leave 20 minutes earlier and the suggestion is exactly 20 minutes before the entered time, including a preceding calendar date.
Saved prediction results cannot be updated or deleted.
Result list optional crowding filter is exact. Default and filtered ordering is journey_date ascending, planned_departure_time ascending, then id ascending.
Invalid creates or edits return field-level errors and make no partial change; rejected edits preserve the prior record.
UI screens:

Application shell with an informational Delhi Metro Planning View selector.
Station setup list and create, edit, and delete controls.
Timetable-pattern setup list and create, edit, and delete controls.
Public-holiday setup list and create, edit, and delete controls.
Journey planner with station selectors, date, time, and prediction result.
Saved prediction-results list with crowding-level filter.
UI states:

Loading state for API-backed lists and selectors.
Empty setup state and disabled dependent actions when prerequisite stations or patterns are unavailable.
Inline validation state retaining entered values and identifying invalid, duplicate, overlap, identical-station, or deletion-reference errors.
No prediction available state without advisory.
Matched Low or Medium state with journey facts, derived day type, and crowding level only.
Matched High state with journey facts, derived day type, crowding level, Leave 20 minutes earlier text, and suggested date and time.
Saved-results empty state and filtered no-results state.
Interaction flows:

Station setup loads records, submits create or edit, refreshes after success, and retains values with errors after failure; delete succeeds only when not referenced.
Timetable setup loads stations and patterns, submits required pair, day type, time range, and crowding, then displays returned record or validation errors.
Holiday setup submits date and display name, refreshes on success, or displays retained-form validation errors.
Journey planner submits distinct stations, date, and time; it displays no-match status or a matched saved prediction and renders advisory only for High.
Results list requests chronological saved predictions with optional exact crowding filter and renders list, empty state, or filtered no-results state.
API endpoints:

GET /api/stations — Order by trimmed name then id ascending.Empty items indicate no stations.
POST /api/stations — 422 for blank or duplicate name.; Store trimmed name.
PUT /api/stations/{id} — 404 if absent.; 422 preserves existing record for invalid or duplicate name.
DELETE /api/stations/{id} — 404 if absent.; 409 if referenced by a timetable pattern.
GET /api/timetable-patterns — Order by origin name, destination name, day type, start time, then id.; Empty items indicate no patterns.
POST /api/timetable-patterns — 422 for unknown or identical stations, invalid fields, invalid ordering, or inclusive overlap.
PUT /api/timetable-patterns/{id} — 404 if absent.; 422 preserves existing record for invalid input or inclusive overlap.
DELETE /api/timetable-patterns/{id} — 404 if absent.
GET /api/public-holidays — Order by calendar_date then id ascending. Empty items indicate no holidays.
POST /api/public-holidays — 422 for invalid date, blank name, or duplicate date.
PUT /api/public-holidays/{id} — 404 if absent.422 preserves the existing record for invalid or duplicate values.
DELETE /api/public-holidays/{id} — 404 if absent.
POST /api/journey-predictions — 422 with field errors for missing, invalid, unknown, or identical stations.; No match returns prediction_available false with nullable result fields and saves nothing.; Match saves a snapshot; advisory fields are populated only for High.
GET /api/saved-prediction-results — Order by journey_date, planned_departure_time, then id ascending.Empty items support both empty-history and filtered-no-results states.; No update or delete endpoint exists for immutable saved results.
